{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You shall not see your brother's donkey.</b> In the parashah of Mishpatim (Exodus 23:5) Scripture mentions כי תראה חמור שונאך — 'when you see the donkey of your enemy' — and here it says חמור אחיך — 'your brother's donkey' — to teach you that even if he is your enemy, when your brother returns to the matter of assistance and you stand with him, you shall forget the hatred and remember the love."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:03.219366462Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}